Fakir said he'd write it, but I had to go get all impatient and do that.

76
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,520
Hello?

77
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,520
What?

78
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:17,520
Mr. Fakir from the ballet division, you want to check out these five books?

79
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:18,520
Yes.

80
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,520
Oh, and that book over there.

81
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,520
What?

82
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:23,520
I was asked to give it to you if you came.

83
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:25,520
To me?

84
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,520
Mr. Altor from the music division asked me.

85
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:28,520
I don't know him.

86
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:31,520
Oh, you know what? I thought so.

87
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,520
What is it?

88
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:36,520
Nothing much. It's strange, but Mr. Altor has borrowed all five of these books before.

89
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,520
What?

90
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:38,520
Whoa!

91
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:41,520
Altor? Who is he?

92
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:46,520
All right then, everybody. I'll pass them out in turn, so please line up.

93
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:51,520
Hey, Doug, you look like you're spacing out. I bet you were so happy you couldn't sleep last night, huh?

94
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,520
Huh? Happy about what?

95
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:57,520
Oh, she's always spaced out, but we'll let it go.

96
00:05:57,520 --> 00:06:01,520
Because today's her long-awaited first point lesson.

97
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:03,520
Point lesson? Is it really?

98
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:07,520
Point! What every girl dreams from the day that she decides to become a ballerina.

99
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:11,520
The long four days of broken nails and painful blood blisters.

100
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:12,520
Correct!

101
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:17,520
And that's why I can't have you taking the flippant attitude that leads to talking in class. You hear me?

102
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,520
Yes, sir!

103
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:22,520
Now, Miss Lillier, your toe shoes.

104
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:23,520
Sir!

105
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,520
Finally, toe shoes.

106
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,520
Sir!

107
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:30,520
When I'm 2-2, I can do point like it's no big deal.

108
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:36,520
But I wonder if the day will come when I can dance a pas de deux with the prince like that while I'm duck.

109
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:37,520
Miss Duck!

110
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:38,520
Yes, sir!

111
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:43,520
I am sorry, but at the moment I'm afraid I can't give you toe shoes.

112
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:44,520
Huh?

113
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:51,520
Your concentration, Miss Duck, has been lacking even more than before. As if you've even lost your eagerness.

114
00:06:52,520 --> 00:07:01,520
Is it possible you've come to the conclusion that you can't do anything, and so as a result, you've decided to stop trying to move forward altogether?

115
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:11,520
Um, well, I... If I really could help Muto by myself, Akira, I wouldn't be asking you. But right now, I can't do anything.

116
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:14,520
What can I do?

117
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:24,520
I'm worried. I truly am worried. I fear your desire to marry me has caused you to be deliberately remiss about your lesson!

118
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:30,520
N-nonsense! Marrying you is too great of an honor! Duck would be afraid to even think of it!

119
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:37,520
Miss Duck, please watch everyone else's practice today!

120
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:38,520
Yes, sir!

121
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:42,520
I'm gonna die!

122
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:47,520
So this is the pain of point, huh? I wish Duck could share this!

123
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:54,520
I'm always watching. Even when Fakir's trying hard, I'm just watching. Maybe that dream was prophetic.

124
00:07:54,520 --> 00:08:00,520
A guy from the music division? What's this about?

125
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:02,520
What's this about?

126
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,520
Shhhh!

127
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,520
You're late.

128
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:13,520
It took you 18 days, 7 hours and 24 minutes.

129
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:15,520
What are you talking about?

130
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:20,520
That's how long it took from the time you began to research your power until you noticed me.

131
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:25,520
Mr. Fakir.

132
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:29,520
I take it your outdoor, then? What is this about?

133
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:36,520
Assumed you hadn't read it, so I set it aside. I think you'll find it useful for when you start writing your stories.

134
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:39,520
Oh, really? And what do you know?

135
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:42,520
Huh. Everything you've been dying to know.

136
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,520
What?

137
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,520
What?

138
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:53,520
Huh? Who was that?

139
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:02,520
I'm asking you who you are?

140
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:05,520
You're as short-tempered as everyone says you are.

141
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:07,520
But remember this.

142
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:10,520
Brute force has no power in the face of words.

143
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:14,520
You want Drosselmeyer's power because you're also aware of that truth, yes?

144
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:16,520
Drosselmeyer's power?

145
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:19,520
The power to make stories into reality.

146
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:21,520
It's splendid.

147
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:26,520
And the books that have had their endings stolen by those who wish to stop them from becoming reality.

148
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:28,520
Isn't it thrilling?

149
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:31,520
You mean they took out the endings to stop them from becoming real?

150
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,520
Yes.

151
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:37,520
Even though the originals are sealed away, and all we can get ahold of are the copies.

152
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:42,520
Imagine, a power so strong those endings still had to be torn out.

153
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:47,520
If you're serious about attaining that power, I wouldn't mind helping you.

154
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:50,520
But you will have to follow my every order.

155
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,520
And be prepared to die if you should fail.

156
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,520
What do you mean?

157
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:58,520
Follow my every order and be prepared to die?

158
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:02,520
What the heck are you talking about? Why should he have to do those things, huh?

159
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:04,520
I am giving him a warning.

160
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,520
Do not take Drosselmeyer's power lightly.

161
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:10,520
If you use it improperly, there will be hell to pay.

162
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:13,520
People may even die.

163
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:18,520
You need to be prepared for that possibility.

164
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:21,520
If you want out, I won't force you.

165
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:23,520
No. Teach me.

166
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,520
But Kier…

167
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:26,520
It's a wise decision.

168
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,520
Come to my house tomorrow.

169
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:29,520
I'll be waiting for Kier.

170
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:33,520
He is awakened.

171
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:35,520
This is dangerous.

172
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:37,520
We must take steps far.

173
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:39,520
Let us kill him.

174
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,520
Now, now, hold on.

175
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:45,520
It seems he's gained the knowledge, but that's all.

176
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:50,520
It wouldn't be a bad thing for us to watch for a little longer.

177
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:55,520
Nothing could be better than if this matter settled itself without mishap.

178
00:10:55,520 --> 00:11:02,520
But if necessary, we'll take steps when the time comes that we need to do so.

179
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:08,520
Oh dear. They've finally begun to go into action. If they do that, the story will stop.

180
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:13,520
Not good. This is extremely bad news indeed, little duck.

181
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:31,520
Say, Fakir, I've been thinking and I've decided I'm going to help you.

182
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:33,520
Huh?

183
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:43,520
Well, because that's the only thing I can really do right now. So I'm just going to do what I can with all I've got. If there's something I can help you with, tell me, no matter what it is.

184
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:48,520
But isn't there something weird about that Autor guy? I wonder if this is okay.

185
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,520
Weird or not, we have no choice.

186
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:54,520
No entourage.

187
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:57,520
What? You mean me, Mr. Autor? I just…

188
00:11:58,520 --> 00:11:59,520
I won't repeat myself.

189
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:05,520
Things relating to Drosselmeyer are gathered inside this house. It is a holy place.

190
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,520
Are you the weird Autor, Zura?

191
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:14,520
People like you two who are totally unrelated aren't allowed inside. Now, come, Fakir.

192
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:17,520
What unrelated?

193
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:19,520
Please take Uzura and go home.

194
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:25,520
Good luck, Fakir.

195
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:35,520
This is Drosselmeyer's study, perfectly recreated from the data I gathered. Paper made from ten-year-old reeds, blue and black ink at a seven-to-three ratio.

196
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:43,520
The feather of a white swan that's crossed the sea three times is best for the pen, but for this pen, I substituted a duck's feather.

197
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:45,520
So then…

198
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:48,520
What was that for?

199
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:50,520
Ritual ablutions.

200
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:55,520
They say Drosselmeyer always cleansed his body with water before he wrote his stories.

201
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:56,520
Didn't you know?

202
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:57,520
Why should I?

203
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:01,520
A direct descendant of Drosselmeyer's? And this is your level?

204
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:04,520
A direct descendant of Drosselmeyer?

205
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:13,520
Oh, no. You're not going to say you didn't know that either, are you? It's a fact about yourself. You really take the cake.

206
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:18,520
This is a Drosselmeyer family tree that I drew after my own research.

207
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:23,520
Look, Drosselmeyer is here, and here you are.

208
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:29,520
I believe I'm probably connected this way from this branch, but I don't have all the evidence yet.

209
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:36,520
But the one who helped my father when he was lost as a boy is this person written here. I know that much.

210
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:46,520
I have Drosselmeyer's blood. Does that mean those books missing their endings are things that Drosselmeyer wrote?

211
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:51,520
And the fact that I saw one of those endings is…

212
00:13:51,520 --> 00:14:08,520
Fakir hasn't come back from Outdoor's house since then. I'm… I'm just waiting.

213
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:11,520
Everybody, pay attention!

214
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:17,520
Today, Miss Roo and Mr. Muto will demonstrate the art of dance partnering.

215
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:29,520
All of you, please watch Miss Roo's point work very closely.

216
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:36,520
I'm just watching again.

217
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:50,520
Roo…

218
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:55,520
That hurts!

219
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:05,520
Miss Roo, you hesitated to take my hand. Can you really say you loved me?

220
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:07,520
No way!

221
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:09,520
A breakup!

222
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,520
Roo, are you okay?

223
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:15,520
Miss Roo? Mr. Muto, what's wrong? Aren't you two getting…

224
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:27,520
It looks like it was too soon for Mr. Muto to get married. After all, the day may come when special marriage training is necessary.

225
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:41,520
Mr. Muto was always kind to Roo, but he's changing more and more.

226
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:44,520
Vakir! Vakir! Vakir!

227
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:46,520
Would you be quiet?

228
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:48,520
Is Vakir…

229
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,520
Vakir…

230
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:51,520
Vakir?

231
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:57,520
Vakir, hang on! Hang in there! What did you do to him?

232
00:15:58,520 --> 00:15:59,520
Nothing.

233
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:00,520
Vakir…

234
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:04,520
It's true. He's been standing there three days, not eating, not sleeping, nothing.

235
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:06,520
Why did you make him do that?

236
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:07,520
Vakir…

237
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:08,520
Vakir…

238
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:10,520
Vakir.

239
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:11,520
Vakir…

240
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:12,520
Not doing that!

241
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:13,520
Vakir…

242
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:15,520
What did you do to try to stand this way? If he can't even endure this, he's a lost cause.

243
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:16,520
You know, you're horrible!

244
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:17,520
Vakir…

245
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:18,520
I'm fine.

246
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:19,520
Vakir...

247
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:21,520
Vakir…

248
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:22,520
Vakir…

249
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,520
Vakir…

250
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,520
Vakir?

251
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:25,520
Vakir…

252
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:26,520
Vakir…

253
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,520
Vakir…

254
